{
  // Used ONLY by this package's "typecheck" script - deliberately not
  // tsconfig.json (which stays untouched and is what @rollup/plugin-typescript
  // uses for the real build). The two have incompatible needs: tsconfig.json
  // needs a narrow rootDir so `dist/` correctly mirrors `src/`, but the real
  // build never actually needs `react-fatless-form` resolved to source - by
  // the time it runs (within `yarn build`'s topological order), core has
  // already been built moments earlier in the same run, so normal
  // node_modules -> core/package.json -> ./dist resolution already works.
  //
  // Standalone `tsc --noEmit` gets no such benefit, since it's a separate
  // script invocation with no ordering relationship to `build`. It needs
  // `paths` to resolve react-fatless-form straight to core's source instead
  // - but rootDir is enforced against the FULL expanded program (everything
  // reached transitively through an import, not just what `include` lists
  // explicitly), so pairing that `paths` entry with an explicit rootDir
  // fails with TS6059 the moment core's own internal imports pull in files
  // outside packages/web/src. Omitting rootDir here lets it be inferred from
  // the actual file set instead, which - since nothing is ever emitted from
  // this config (--noEmit) - is always safe.
  //
  // Mirrors this package's own jest.config.cjs moduleNameMapper, which
  // already does the equivalent redirect at test time.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "react-fatless-form": ["../core/src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}